WEBVTT

00:04.900 --> 00:06.150
<b>I see.</b>

00:06.690 --> 00:10.110
<b>So the mastermind
behind Hajime Saito was you.</b>

00:10.610 --> 00:12.780
<b>Former Revolutionary warrior
from Satsuma...</b>

00:13.280 --> 00:15.570
<b>and Home Minister
of the Meiji government...</b>

00:15.570 --> 00:17.320
<b>Toshimichi Okubo.</b>

00:22.960 --> 00:26.540
<b>That said, I have no idea who that is!</b>

00:26.540 --> 00:29.750
<b>Of course little kids
who don't read newspapers wouldn't know.</b>

00:30.800 --> 00:34.430
<b>Alongside Takamori Saigo
and Kogoro Katsura,</b>

00:34.430 --> 00:36.890
<b>he's the last of
the Great Trio of the Revolution,</b>

00:36.890 --> 00:39.310
<b>who achieved the most
in the Meiji Revolution.</b>

00:39.810 --> 00:42.730
<b>The leader of the Home Ministry
that controls the entire government.</b>

00:43.310 --> 00:47.190
<b>In other words, he's the minister who sits
at the top of national power in Japan.</b>

00:47.810 --> 00:49.900
<b>Sorry for the rough handling.</b>

00:50.980 --> 00:55.700
<b>But there was a need for us
to know your current strength.</b>

00:56.610 --> 00:58.570
<b>Will you listen to us?</b>

00:59.580 --> 01:02.120
<b>Yeah, even if by force.</b>

01:03.450 --> 01:06.120
<b>Th-This has turned into a huge ordeal.</b>

01:06.120 --> 01:10.250
<b>I didn't think someone as big as Okubo
from the Home Ministry would show up.</b>

01:10.250 --> 01:12.670
<b>It's no time to be talkin'
about Battosai anymore.</b>

01:15.760 --> 01:18.470
<b>Hmph. What a wet blanket.</b>

01:18.470 --> 01:21.260
<b>I'll have to leave settling this score
for our next opportunity.</b>

01:21.600 --> 01:23.220
<b>Looks like someone escaped death.</b>

01:23.560 --> 01:24.930
<b>Yeah, you did.</b>

01:30.190 --> 01:31.190
<b>Saito!</b>

01:31.820 --> 01:33.070
<b>Operations report!</b>

01:33.530 --> 01:36.780
<b>Kenshin Himura is completely useless.</b>

01:37.280 --> 01:41.160
<b>However, Himura Battosai
seems to do fairly well.</b>

01:41.370 --> 01:42.280
<b>That is all!</b>

01:43.700 --> 01:45.700
<b>Sheesh, that guy.</b>

01:45.910 --> 01:48.330
<b>He's the best spy
in the Metropolitan Police.</b>

01:48.330 --> 01:51.630
<b>But I just can't figure out
what the Wolf of Mibu is thinking about!</b>

01:52.500 --> 01:54.920
<b>Himura, come with me.</b>

01:54.920 --> 01:56.010
<b>Stop daydreaming.</b>

01:56.300 --> 01:59.180
<b>I'm not the only one
that got roped into—</b>

02:01.180 --> 02:02.010
<b>Kenshin?!</b>

02:06.230 --> 02:10.940
<b>I'm not the only one roped
into this situation, that I'm not.</b>

02:11.360 --> 02:13.940
<b>Everyone here will listen
to what you have to say.</b>

02:14.570 --> 02:15.530
<b>"I"...</b>

02:16.530 --> 02:17.530
<b>Oh...</b>

02:17.780 --> 02:20.700
<b>I'm so glad! You're back
to your normal self, Kenshin!</b>

02:21.200 --> 02:22.370
<b>Oro...</b>

02:23.200 --> 02:24.790
<b>- Miss Megumi, hurry!
- Sir Okubo...</b>

02:24.790 --> 02:27.450
<b>- What are you doing, you idiot!
- Let's do as he says.</b>

02:27.450 --> 02:30.540
<b>Right now, I need Himura's power
more than anything else.</b>

02:29.250 --> 02:30.080
<b>Kenshin!</b>

02:30.080 --> 02:32.880
<b>How long are you gonna be
a stupidly powerful girl?</b>

02:30.670 --> 02:34.000
<b>Oro...</b>

02:32.880 --> 02:34.000
<b>You say that, but...</b>

04:03.930 --> 04:07.930
<b>EPISODE 24:
MEIJI 11, MAY 14TH</b>

04:10.850 --> 04:13.310
<b>Himura, I'll cut to the chase.</b>

04:14.310 --> 04:17.190
<b>Shishio is active
behind the scenes in Kyoto.</b>

04:18.860 --> 04:22.320
<b>You went so straight to the point
that I don't get it, Mr. Okubo.</b>

04:22.320 --> 04:23.990
<b>Who the hell is this Shishio guy?</b>

04:23.990 --> 04:26.160
<b>Hey! Watch your tongue!</b>

04:26.160 --> 04:27.580
<b>Makoto Shishio.</b>

04:28.580 --> 04:31.000
<b>After I accepted the role
of mercenary swordsman</b>

04:31.000 --> 04:33.120
<b>and came out into the limelight
from the shadows,</b>

04:33.370 --> 04:38.250
<b>another Revolutionary warrior from Choshu
took over the role of Shadow Hitokiri.</b>

04:39.130 --> 04:42.880
<b>You could say he is the successor
to Hitokiri Battosai, that he is.</b>

04:44.470 --> 04:49.310
<b>As he completely stayed in the shadows,
very few know of his existence.</b>

04:50.220 --> 04:53.640
<b>Even I, his predecessor, have never
met him in person, that I haven't.</b>

04:54.560 --> 04:56.190
<b>But what does this mean, that is?</b>

04:56.850 --> 05:00.190
<b>I had heard Shisho died ten years ago
during the Boshin War.</b>

05:03.990 --> 05:05.200
<b>I see.</b>

05:05.200 --> 05:07.240
<b>Shishio didn't die.</b>

05:07.240 --> 05:09.780
<b>His existence was eradicated
by his comrades, that it was.</b>

05:12.290 --> 05:15.540
<b>Secretly snuffing out
the one executing shady deeds</b>

05:15.540 --> 05:18.580
<b>that can't ever be leaked
for our own safety.</b>

05:19.880 --> 05:22.510
<b>Back in those days,
it wasn't anything unusual.</b>

05:23.130 --> 05:29.760
<b>Makoto Shishio had just as much talent
as you in sword skill and in quick wits.</b>

05:30.390 --> 05:32.430
<b>But he was also a dangerous one</b>

05:32.430 --> 05:36.230
<b>with incomprehensible levels of ambition
and desire for domination.</b>

05:37.060 --> 05:39.520
<b>He accepted the role of Shadow Hitokiri</b>

05:39.520 --> 05:42.400
<b>only to display his talent
and existence to the world.</b>

05:43.280 --> 05:45.740
<b>Some of the assassinations
Shishio committed</b>

05:45.740 --> 05:49.870
<b>would overturn the Meiji government
from its foundation.</b>

05:50.660 --> 05:53.990
<b>If we were to ring in the new era
with Shishio still alive,</b>

05:53.990 --> 05:56.830
<b>he would take advantage of such weakness
and become arrogant</b>

05:57.330 --> 05:59.710
<b>We might even end up
with the entirety of Japan</b>

05:59.710 --> 06:01.630
<b>becoming a plaything for just Shishio.</b>

06:01.960 --> 06:06.590
<b>That's why you killed him in the chaos
of the Boshin War, that you did?</b>

06:07.590 --> 06:09.510
<b>Right. We definitely killed him.</b>

06:10.470 --> 06:13.260
<b>We even had oil poured on his corpse
and lit it on fire.</b>

06:14.560 --> 06:18.230
<b>However, even with his entire body
engulfed in flames,</b>

06:18.230 --> 06:20.270
<b>Makoto Shishio was still alive.</b>

06:21.230 --> 06:25.940
<b>And now he has taken a multitude
of treasonous subordinates under his wing</b>

06:25.940 --> 06:27.990
<b>to create a giant army</b>

06:27.990 --> 06:33.620
<b>and has made a base in Kyoto to plot a war
that splits this nation in two as revenge.</b>

06:35.240 --> 06:39.000
<b>Countless squads we sent in
to take him down have been eradicated.</b>

06:39.580 --> 06:42.630
<b>You are the only one left
that we can count on.</b>

06:43.630 --> 06:46.800
<b>It's for the people
of this country, Himura.</b>

06:47.300 --> 06:49.510
<b>I want you to head to Kyoto once more.</b>

06:52.550 --> 06:53.800
<b>In other words...</b>

06:54.260 --> 06:58.270
<b>are you saying you want Kenshin
to assassinate Makoto Shishio?</b>

06:59.730 --> 07:01.480
<b>That's what it would mean, yes.</b>

07:01.690 --> 07:03.810
<b>We will pay more than enough in reward.</b>

07:04.020 --> 07:06.530
<b>On top of that,
we will go outside the law</b>

07:06.530 --> 07:08.860
<b>and overlook
all of your previous illegal activities.</b>

07:08.860 --> 07:13.120
<b>For instance, we can acquit Megumi Takani
from her illicit sales of opium.</b>

07:13.620 --> 07:14.990
<b>You've got to be kidding me.</b>

07:15.530 --> 07:19.250
<b>If you're going to use me for negotiation,
turning me into shackles for Ken-san,</b>

07:19.540 --> 07:22.710
<b>I would rather choose the gallows.</b>

07:24.130 --> 07:28.630
<b>Basically, all of this
is because of your nasty doings, right?</b>

07:29.130 --> 07:32.260
<b>And you want Kenshin
to clean up your mess?</b>

07:32.260 --> 07:34.640
<b>Ain't you askin' for a bit much?</b>

07:34.890 --> 07:37.100
<b>Ignorant youngsters keep out of this!</b>

07:37.100 --> 07:39.480
<b>The Meiji government
is on the brink of extinction!</b>

07:39.730 --> 07:42.770
<b>Filthy governments
can go ahead and become extinct.</b>

07:43.190 --> 07:47.900
<b>Though, I don't like how people living
ordinary lives are troubled by all of it.</b>

07:47.900 --> 07:50.280
<b>Without the prosperity
of the Meiji government,</b>

07:50.280 --> 07:52.820
<b>the people cannot be at peace, idiot!</b>

07:52.820 --> 07:55.200
<b>And that's where you guys
are being conceited!</b>

07:55.200 --> 07:56.700
<b>If you keep spouting nonsense,</b>

07:56.700 --> 07:58.740
<b>- I'll arrest you!
- Try me, Mr. Huge Forehead!</b>

07:58.740 --> 08:01.370
<b>I'm just a kid,
so I don't get it too well.</b>

08:02.210 --> 08:05.040
<b>But I can understand
that if things had gone wrong,</b>

08:05.040 --> 08:08.300
<b>Kenshin may have been eradicated
just like Shishio.</b>

08:08.880 --> 08:10.210
<b>Both then and now,</b>

08:10.210 --> 08:13.510
<b>you guys are assassinating
and eradicating for your own purposes.</b>

08:14.050 --> 08:16.890
<b>All you old guys are a bit crazy.</b>

08:18.430 --> 08:19.350
<b>Sir Okubo.</b>

08:20.220 --> 08:25.020
<b>I understand that you are all in need
of Hitokiri Battosai right now.</b>

08:25.480 --> 08:28.520
<b>But the current Kenshin
is a rurouni who refuses to kill.</b>

08:29.650 --> 08:32.860
<b>We will never, ever
let Kenshin go to Kyoto!</b>

08:37.530 --> 08:40.580
<b>Are you all stupid?! Do you not understand
just how dire the situation—</b>

08:40.580 --> 08:42.200
<b>Stop it, Kawaji.</b>

08:45.790 --> 08:48.170
<b>Think about it for a week.</b>

08:48.590 --> 08:53.880
<b>In one week, on May 14th,
I will come again to hear your answer.</b>

08:58.550 --> 08:59.600
<b>Mr. Okubo.</b>

09:01.810 --> 09:04.940
<b>You have gotten quite haggard
compared to a decade ago.</b>

09:06.310 --> 09:11.900
<b>It is far more difficult to establish
a new era than to break an old one.</b>

09:12.570 --> 09:13.650
<b>That's what this means.</b>

09:14.570 --> 09:16.780
<b>I'm looking forward
to a favorable reply from you.</b>

09:25.160 --> 09:26.920
<b>Toshimichi Okubo?!</b>

09:27.120 --> 09:30.000
<b>I'm gonna bail and head to Shanghai,
where it's safe!</b>

09:30.290 --> 09:31.420
<b>Got that?</b>

09:31.420 --> 09:34.470
<b>There is a safer place to escape to
than Shanghai.</b>

09:38.180 --> 09:40.300
<b>A place called hell.</b>

09:42.310 --> 09:48.020
<b>It seems all you Imperialists think you
created the Meiji Era all by yourselves.</b>

09:48.400 --> 09:50.940
<b>But we on the Shogunate side
risked our lives</b>

09:50.940 --> 09:54.740
<b>for the foundation of Meiji
through the role of the losers.</b>

09:55.320 --> 09:58.320
<b>I'm obedient to the government as a spy</b>

09:58.320 --> 10:01.490
<b>so I can eradicate
the mites that feed upon Meiji</b>

10:01.490 --> 10:05.120
<b>as an obligation of the Shinsengumi
who lived on into the Meiji Era.</b>

10:06.040 --> 10:09.710
<b>Okubo or otherwise,
if they drown in self-interest</b>

10:09.710 --> 10:12.630
<b>and bring calamities
to the people of this nation,</b>

10:12.630 --> 10:15.380
<b>I will slay them under the doctrine
of Evil-Immediate-Slaughter.</b>

10:15.630 --> 10:18.220
<b>W-Wait. I can pay as much as you want.</b>

10:18.840 --> 10:21.140
<b>You can own a dog with food.</b>

10:21.140 --> 10:23.350
<b>You can own people with money.</b>

10:23.350 --> 10:27.810
<b>But nobody can own
the Wolves of Mibu.</b>

10:35.150 --> 10:36.990
<b>A wolf is a wolf.</b>

10:37.440 --> 10:39.740
<b>The Shinsengumi is the Shinsengumi.</b>

10:40.740 --> 10:44.200
<b>And a hitokiri is a hitokiri.</b>

10:46.450 --> 10:49.000
<b>Right, Battosai?</b>

10:50.960 --> 10:53.960
<b>RUROUNI KENSHIN</b>

10:54.500 --> 10:57.670
<b>MEIJI 11, MAY 14TH</b>

11:02.550 --> 11:04.560
<b>There. Spotless!</b>

11:04.560 --> 11:06.020
<b>- Hey.
- Oro!</b>

11:07.220 --> 11:09.140
<b>I thought I was going to die, that I did.</b>

11:09.640 --> 11:12.650
<b>This isn't time
to be leisurely doing your laundry.</b>

11:12.650 --> 11:14.230
<b>What's your answer gonna be?</b>

11:14.520 --> 11:17.150
<b>I say don't do such a shady deal.</b>

11:17.150 --> 11:21.450
<b>The leader of the government
that is addicted to personal gain</b>

11:21.700 --> 11:23.660
<b>can't be trusted at all.</b>

11:24.910 --> 11:26.830
<b>Sano, you really detest
the Meiji government</b>

11:26.830 --> 11:28.660
<b>from the bottom of your heart,
that you do.</b>

11:28.870 --> 11:30.620
<b>I do. Got a problem?</b>

11:31.120 --> 11:36.380
<b>No. But if Sir Okubo was one that would
be acting only out of self-interest,</b>

11:37.130 --> 11:39.630
<b>Saito would have slain him long ago,
that he would have.</b>

11:41.180 --> 11:43.180
<b>That punk officer would have?</b>

11:43.510 --> 11:45.180
<b>He's a government dog, ain't he?</b>

11:46.140 --> 11:51.390
<b>Before he fought me, Saito definitely
uttered the word "justice."</b>

11:51.980 --> 11:56.020
<b>One who has sunken to become a dog
in both mind and body</b>

11:56.020 --> 11:57.440
<b>would never utter such a word.</b>

11:58.150 --> 12:01.780
<b>That man is still
one of the Wolves of Mibu to this day.</b>

12:02.530 --> 12:05.990
<b>He bares his fangs
of Evil-Immediate-Slaughter</b>

12:05.990 --> 12:08.410
<b>in the darkness
where the sun doesn't shine.</b>

12:09.620 --> 12:13.250
<b>That said, he's not someone
I can become friendly with, that he isn't.</b>

12:13.460 --> 12:14.460
<b>Right!</b>

12:14.460 --> 12:15.580
<b>Of course not!</b>

12:15.580 --> 12:16.420
<b>I hate him!</b>

12:20.300 --> 12:22.170
<b>Oh, my, Mr. Fujita. So filthy!</b>

12:22.880 --> 12:23.880
<b>Excuse me.</b>

12:24.510 --> 12:27.810
<b>Four times.
Looks like I have gathered much hatred.</b>

12:28.640 --> 12:33.230
<b>Ah, well. It is the destiny
Of the Shinsengumi to be hated in any era.</b>

12:34.270 --> 12:36.020
<b>MEIJI 11, MAY 14TH</b>

12:35.190 --> 12:36.020
<b>Now...</b>

12:36.980 --> 12:39.730
<b>what's your move, Battosai?</b>

12:43.650 --> 12:47.200
<b>I will head right now
to go see Sir Okubo, that I will.</b>

12:48.330 --> 12:51.370
<b>Why? If I recall,
he said he would come over.</b>

12:51.580 --> 12:55.040
<b>Sir Okubo is quite a busy man, that he is.</b>

12:55.370 --> 12:57.380
<b>- Besides—
- There you are.</b>

12:57.880 --> 12:59.250
<b>Good morning, Ken-san.</b>

12:59.590 --> 13:01.840
<b>Today is the day
you're going to give your answer.</b>

13:02.260 --> 13:03.840
<b>It's been on my mind, so I came here.</b>

13:04.090 --> 13:09.100
<b>I thank you for that. But I am about
to head out right now, that I am.</b>

13:09.100 --> 13:10.100
<b>Huh?</b>

13:10.100 --> 13:12.810
<b>Do you know where Okubo's mansion is?</b>

13:12.810 --> 13:17.100
<b>No. But I did hear
that he was headed for Dajokan in Akasaka,</b>

13:17.100 --> 13:20.400
<b>so I will likely bump into him if I headed
over to the Kioizaka area, that I should.</b>

13:20.610 --> 13:22.440
<b>Then we should go, too—</b>

13:22.820 --> 13:25.910
<b>No, this will likely be
a very complicated conversation,</b>

13:25.910 --> 13:27.450
<b>so I prefer to go alone, that I do.</b>

13:30.620 --> 13:31.620
<b>It's okay.</b>

13:31.990 --> 13:34.710
<b>Kenshin won't leave you behind
and run off to Kyoto.</b>

13:35.210 --> 13:39.210
<b>That's right. There's no way he'd lend
a hand to assassination after all this.</b>

13:39.710 --> 13:42.050
<b>I'll never let him go.</b>

13:45.050 --> 13:45.970
<b><i>Kenshin...</i></b>

13:52.720 --> 13:56.230
<b><i>Will Himura actually
perform an action for us?</i></b>

13:57.770 --> 14:01.150
<b><i>No, I need him to,
no matter what the cost.</i></b>

14:03.570 --> 14:06.990
<b>If Himura doesn't act,
this country will fall to ruin.</b>

14:09.320 --> 14:14.330
<b>The fate of this nation is something a man
who is about to die need not worry about.</b>

14:15.790 --> 14:16.790
<b>Wha—</b>

14:18.040 --> 14:19.880
<b>A message from Mr. Shishio.</b>

14:21.250 --> 14:23.170
<b>"It was quite a brilliant idea</b>

14:23.170 --> 14:25.920
<b>to try sending Himura Battosai
as an assassin,</b>

14:26.420 --> 14:28.510
<b>but ultimately a futile resistance.</b>

14:28.760 --> 14:32.260
<b>I will take this country for myself,"
so he says.</b>

14:37.850 --> 14:40.520
<b>I am a samurai from Ishikawa,
Ichiro Shimada!</b>

14:40.520 --> 14:42.400
<b>Likewise, Tsurahide Cho!</b>

14:42.400 --> 14:44.480
<b>Hateful villain Okubo, brace yourself!</b>

14:47.070 --> 14:48.030
<b>Okubo!</b>

14:49.740 --> 14:52.320
<b>H-He's been murdered.</b>

14:53.080 --> 14:55.160
<b>Who would do this before us?</b>

14:55.660 --> 14:58.250
<b>We have already sent
the vindication notes of assassination</b>

14:58.250 --> 14:59.960
<b>to the government and the press already.</b>

15:00.540 --> 15:02.540
<b>This is just how it's gonna be.</b>

15:03.090 --> 15:05.460
<b>We were the ones that killed Okubo.</b>

15:05.960 --> 15:07.300
<b>Shimada!</b>

15:09.300 --> 15:10.970
<b>There are no witnesses!</b>

15:10.970 --> 15:13.390
<b>The seven of us killed Okubo!</b>

15:15.220 --> 15:17.350
<b>Y-Yeah!</b>

15:18.480 --> 15:23.400
<b><i>Meiji 11, May 14th.
The Kioizaka Incident.</i></b>

15:23.860 --> 15:26.230
<b><i>The great case of the man
reigning at the top of Meiji</i></b>

15:26.230 --> 15:28.570
<b><i>being assassinated in broad daylight</i></b>

15:28.570 --> 15:32.110
<b><i>thus became the deed
of a group of assassins</i></b>

15:32.110 --> 15:34.580
<b><i>with Ishiakwa samurais at the core,</i></b>

15:34.580 --> 15:38.540
<b><i>and the existence of Shishio and his group
did not come out into the open.</i></b>

15:40.290 --> 15:41.540
<b>Mr. Okubo...</b>

15:42.580 --> 15:46.250
<b>It's in your best interests
to not oppose Mr. Shishio as well.</b>

15:53.260 --> 15:55.100
<b><i>Makoto Shishio.</i></b>

15:57.100 --> 15:59.100
<b>This is how Shishio does things!</b>

15:59.640 --> 16:01.690
<b>They never come out into the open,</b>

16:01.690 --> 16:03.770
<b>and until that day
where everyone riots at once,</b>

16:03.770 --> 16:06.650
<b>they will gradually shave off
the power of the Meiji government!</b>

16:08.110 --> 16:09.400
<b>Sir Okubo...</b>

16:11.950 --> 16:13.320
<b>Excuse me.</b>

16:13.530 --> 16:16.080
<b>Governor of Fukushima, Sir Yamayoshi.</b>

16:16.700 --> 16:19.910
<b>He is the last person to have
a conversation with Sir Okubo.</b>

16:20.290 --> 16:22.750
<b>After finishing
my business meetings in Tokyo,</b>

16:23.040 --> 16:26.590
<b>I went to the Okubo mansion
for final greetings this morning.</b>

16:28.590 --> 16:30.920
<b>It has already
been ten years since the Revolution.</b>

16:31.630 --> 16:33.510
<b>If you ask me what I have achieved,</b>

16:33.510 --> 16:35.850
<b>it's embarrassing to say,
but I have very few results.</b>

16:36.350 --> 16:38.060
<b>But this is where things begin.</b>

16:39.270 --> 16:43.890
<b>To solidify the foundation of a nation,
you need 30 years' worth of time.</b>

16:44.400 --> 16:45.440
<b>The ten years until now</b>

16:45.440 --> 16:48.230
<b>have been the first phase,
the time for establishment.</b>

16:48.770 --> 16:51.190
<b>The next ten years
will be time for development.</b>

16:51.690 --> 16:54.740
<b>We will tidy up internal affairs
and enrich this nation.</b>

16:55.410 --> 16:57.700
<b>These are the most important times.</b>

16:58.280 --> 17:04.370
<b>Though unworthy, I would like to carry out
those middle ten years at any cost.</b>

17:05.170 --> 17:08.130
<b>I will leave the third and final years
of building and maintaining</b>

17:08.130 --> 17:09.550
<b>to the younger generation</b>

17:09.550 --> 17:11.170
<b>and at the same time set up a congress</b>

17:11.170 --> 17:13.380
<b>to shift our government
into a civil government.</b>

17:14.090 --> 17:17.680
<b>Japan will then be reborn
as a nation-state,</b>

17:18.180 --> 17:20.720
<b>and the revolution
will reach true completion.</b>

17:22.430 --> 17:23.890
<b>"Nation-state."</b>

17:24.560 --> 17:25.900
<b>Nation-state, you say.</b>

17:26.770 --> 17:29.770
<b>A nation where the citizens
choose their own path,</b>

17:30.270 --> 17:33.280
<b>unlike the past,
where authorities decided on everything.</b>

17:34.530 --> 17:36.780
<b>Way too magnificent an ideal.</b>

17:37.030 --> 17:39.870
<b>But it was an ideal worth believing in.</b>

17:41.120 --> 17:43.790
<b>Only if Sir Okubo
was still alive and well.</b>

17:45.040 --> 17:46.540
<b>Extra! Extra!</b>

17:47.040 --> 17:49.960
<b>Lord Okubo was assassinated!
Home Minister's assassination!</b>

17:49.960 --> 17:52.130
<b>Extra! Extra!</b>

17:52.130 --> 17:54.920
<b>Thus, the last
of the Great Trio of the Revolution</b>

17:54.920 --> 17:56.930
<b>and biggest leader was lost,</b>

17:57.430 --> 18:01.510
<b>and the government is left with only scum
who are unfit to serve the role.</b>

18:03.640 --> 18:07.650
<b>Japan will surely stray off its tracks
from now on.</b>

18:08.100 --> 18:11.820
<b>And Shishio
will never let this chance slip by.</b>

18:13.730 --> 18:17.280
<b><i>The times are starting to flow once again.</i></b>

18:22.030 --> 18:24.750
<b>Of all nights, tonight is when
I have an emergency patient.</b>

18:25.750 --> 18:27.500
<b>I'll walk her down to the station.</b>

18:27.870 --> 18:29.540
<b>Yeah. Please be careful.</b>

18:34.760 --> 18:37.090
<b><i>Kenshin sure is late.</i></b>

18:39.930 --> 18:40.890
<b>Kenshin!</b>

18:47.600 --> 18:48.640
<b>Where's Yahiko?</b>

18:49.310 --> 18:50.770
<b>Oh, um...</b>

18:50.770 --> 18:52.820
<b>right, he got tired of waiting
and fell asleep.</b>

18:53.270 --> 18:54.280
<b>I see.</b>

18:55.610 --> 18:56.530
<b>Kenshin?</b>

18:57.610 --> 18:59.990
<b>Sir Okubo was murdered this morning.</b>

19:00.490 --> 19:02.700
<b>Yes. I know from the extra.</b>

19:04.030 --> 19:06.250
<b>The true culprit is Shishio, that it is.</b>

19:08.120 --> 19:11.130
<b>I can't leave Shishio at large like this.</b>

19:12.130 --> 19:14.590
<b>I will be heading to Kyoto, that I will.</b>

19:19.260 --> 19:22.180
<b>Are you going to assassinate
Makoto Shishio?</b>

19:22.680 --> 19:23.510
<b>No...</b>

19:24.260 --> 19:25.930
<b>but I don't know.</b>

19:27.810 --> 19:31.600
<b>After coming here,
so many calming days continued...</b>

19:32.100 --> 19:37.940
<b>I felt like I could really change into an
ordinary swordsman instead of a manslayer.</b>

19:39.450 --> 19:43.200
<b>However, I had a realization
during my battle with Saito.</b>

19:43.910 --> 19:46.490
<b>At the bottom of my heart,</b>

19:46.490 --> 19:51.120
<b>there resides an insane hitokiri
who will never change his ways.</b>

19:52.040 --> 19:54.130
<b>But you come back so quickly!</b>

19:54.130 --> 19:56.630
<b>No matter how close you get
to being Battosai, Kenshin,</b>

19:56.630 --> 19:57.760
<b>you're still Kenshin!</b>

19:58.090 --> 20:01.470
<b>It was the same way
with Jine and with Saito!</b>

20:01.970 --> 20:03.010
<b>You'll be fine!</b>

20:03.840 --> 20:05.180
<b>It was different, that it was.</b>

20:06.470 --> 20:09.270
<b>For Jine's case, I reverted to Battosai</b>

20:09.270 --> 20:11.810
<b>as I wholeheartedly wanted
to save you, Miss Kaoru.</b>

20:11.810 --> 20:14.520
<b>I was able to return to myself
with your voice as well.</b>

20:14.770 --> 20:19.320
<b>But in Saito's case,
I had reverted sheerly to fight.</b>

20:20.610 --> 20:23.700
<b>And your voice did not reach me at all.</b>

20:24.870 --> 20:26.700
<b>There is a crucial difference there.</b>

20:28.950 --> 20:31.460
<b>The times have started to flow again.</b>

20:33.040 --> 20:35.000
<b>When we first met,
you kept me from leaving</b>

20:35.000 --> 20:37.630
<b>despite knowing the fact
that I was Hitokiri Battosai.</b>

20:38.130 --> 20:43.510
<b>You said, "I'm not particular
about people's pasts."</b>

20:44.010 --> 20:48.470
<b>That made me really happy.</b>

20:50.310 --> 20:59.280
<b>KAMIYA KASSHIN
SCHOOL OF KENDO</b>

20:50.720 --> 20:52.980
<b>If I stay here any longer,</b>

20:52.980 --> 20:56.560
<b>I will rope all of you into danger
at every single opportunity,</b>

20:56.560 --> 21:00.610
<b>and each time,
I will return to being Battosai.</b>

21:01.400 --> 21:04.700
<b>Furthermore, for government officials
and the Shisho clan,</b>

21:04.700 --> 21:06.240
<b>and for everyone
across this nation</b>

21:06.240 --> 21:07.120
<b>with a grudge</b>

21:07.120 --> 21:08.240
<b>against
Hitokiri Battosai,</b>

21:08.240 --> 21:09.700
<b>which I feel
there are many of,</b>

21:09.700 --> 21:12.830
<b>I am no person other than Battosai.</b>

21:13.750 --> 21:15.080
<b>I am not allowed</b>

21:15.080 --> 21:16.580
<b>to remain here
any longer.</b>

21:22.170 --> 21:23.510
<b>Thank you for everything.</b>

21:24.260 --> 21:25.090
<b>And...</b>

21:26.430 --> 21:27.340
<b>farewell.</b>

21:28.970 --> 21:30.470
<b>I am a rurouni.</b>

21:31.180 --> 21:33.890
<b>I will wander once again, that I will.</b>

21:48.570 --> 21:50.240
<b>Ken... shin.</b>

21:56.710 --> 21:59.880
<b>Kenshin!</b>

22:00.960 --> 22:04.420
<b><i>Meiji 11, May 14th.</i></b>

22:04.800 --> 22:09.140
<b><i>On this day, Kenshin Himura
returned to being a rurouni</i></b>

22:09.140 --> 22:13.560
<b><i>and disappeared alone
into the pitch-black shadows.</i></b>

22:15.230 --> 22:17.190
<b><i>Where did Battosai disappear to?</i></b>

22:17.690 --> 22:20.900
<b><i>I'll take that Japanese katana
in lieu of money!</i></b>

22:21.520 --> 22:25.070
<b><i>You decide to nonchalantly
show up after all this time.</i></b>

22:25.740 --> 22:27.570
<b><i>What do you want with me?</i></b>

22:28.070 --> 22:30.280
<b><i>Mr. Shishio has been expecting you.</i></b>

22:30.780 --> 22:32.410
<b><i>Now, please.</i></b>

22:33.740 --> 22:38.000
<b><i>So you're... Makoto Shisho, that you are?</i></b>

22:40.210 --> 22:42.210
<b><i>You can at least add an honorific.</i></b>

22:42.710 --> 22:44.630
<b><i>What a rude predecessor.</i></b>
